From 1433ad823739fb2f2bd6b5408061bed249e11f07 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jack Walters <jackwalterswork@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 16:50:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] git_ui: Show and start threads on the merge request
 itself

A thread with no position on the diff was dropped when the threads were
read, so a thread opened on the merge request as a whole never showed,
and there was no way to open one. These threads now sit under the
description, each folded to a line saying who opened it and whether it
is resolved, with reply and resolve buttons once opened. A Start Thread
button in the title row, also the git::StartMergeRequestThread action,
posts a new one at once. Plain comments, which cannot be resolved, stay
out.

The threads were also read from the first page of a hundred discussions
only. Each system note is a discussion of its own, so a busy merge
request passed that long before it had a hundred threads, and the
newest threads were the ones cut off. Every page is read now.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
